#{[17592186385541 #edb/ref 1080 "(4,-2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385541 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385541 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6f89f99e-c222-5f75-b88f-1f3ed3be632f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385542 #edb/ref 1080 "(2,1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385542 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55d2d586-a13f-55b7-99b9-71d0fd4b3d5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186385544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $g(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇g(x,y,z)=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ceb4f40b-ddfe-5165-8e9a-092d10842d64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385543 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+0+0-1-0-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+0-0-1-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =0+0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+z\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}-0-0-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x &=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y &=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=1.$  Similarly, from the second and third equations, we obtain $y=1$ and $z=1.$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=0$ at the point $(1,1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385544 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "12e34691-896f-5bb6-afac-57e259bb49f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385545 #edb/ref 1080 "(0,0,0)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385545 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385545 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00852e0a-f6f6-5c5a-ac0e-5aab7917034a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385546 #edb/ref 1080 "(e,e,e)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385546 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385546 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a138de7-1cdb-5fca-ab9b-192f03014909" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385547 #edb/ref 1080 "(\\frac{1}{e},\\frac{1}{e},\\frac{1}{e})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385547 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385547 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4db23065-4328-5f87-98fa-c2f53e71285d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385548 #edb/ref 1080 "(-1,-1,-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385548 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385548 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c45fae02-a3c6-5e5b-83c3-515185ddf33b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385549 #edb/ref 1080 "(1,1,1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385549 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385549 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "965bb97e-ab1f-5bcd-b8b9-68650da44bfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440312 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440313 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440314 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440315 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440316 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440317 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-1,-1)$\n- **II.** $(-1,-1,1)$\n- **III.** $(-1,1,-1)$\n- **IV.** $(-1,1,1)$\n- **V.** $(1,-1,-1)$\n- **VI.** $(1,1,1)$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c503ae86-f71f-5a21-9c90-e19ce4d410a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403475 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{1}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-1.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}(-1)}{{z}^{2}(-1)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{(-1)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ z+y & =0 \\\\ y & =-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-1$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=1.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(-1,1,-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186428464 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428464 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not 